  <ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock id="HH2FB9527C1D4BB25D79F1C0C76F5BC95D" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;div&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;6. FirstEnergy Pennsylvania Electric Company (FE PA) has authorization from the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) to incur short-term debt of up to $1,250 million through bank facilities and FirstEnergy's regulated money&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;pool, and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;has authorization from the Pennsylvania Public Utility Commission (PPUC) to participate in the regulated money pool. FE PA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;has the ability to&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;borrow from its regulated affiliates and FirstEnergy Corp. (FE) to meet its short-term working capital requirements. FirstEnergy Service Company administers this money pool and tracks surplus funds of FE and the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;respective regulated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;subsidiary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;, as well as proceeds available from bank borrowings. Companies receiving a loan under the money pool agreements must repay the principal amount of the loan, together with accrued interest, within 364 days of borrowing the funds. The rate of interest is the same for each company receiving a loan from their respective pool and is based on the average cost of funds available through the pool. The average interest rate for borrowings for the first three months of 2026 was &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;22&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% per annum.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;In &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;March&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;FE PA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; issued $300 million of 4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% senior unsecured notes due in 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;8 and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;55&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;0 million of 4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;55&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;% senior unsecured notes due in 20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;31&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;. Proceeds were used to refinance existing debt,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; repayment of 5.15% senior notes &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;due in March &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;2026,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt; to finance capital expenditures, for working capital, and for other general corporate purposes.&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:8pt; font-size:8pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;p style="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:12pt"&gt;&#xD;
				&lt;span style="font-family:'Times New Roman'; "&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&#xD;
			&lt;/p&gt;&#xD;
		&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;
	&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfObligationsIncurredOrAssumedByRespondentAsGuarantorForThePerformanceByAnotherOfAnyAgreementOrObligationTextBlock>
